flow` as `natives.patch` has it, and so do the unsigned `NN32` and `NN64` add, subtract, multiply and negate natives beside them (`compile-ladder/rung-overflow-natives/REPORT.md` sections 5-7). *The test.* `XXXFixedWidthOverflowRungB.fss` is now the plain `ProjectFortress/tests/FixedWidthOverflowRungB.fss` (home 1), with the unsigned cases and non-throwing guards added. It passes under walk, through `testSystem` and on the compiled path. `intPrim.fss:31-32` and `longPrim.fss:31-32` assert the raise at the bounds. *The count.* Of 413 interpreter tests, none changed (`compile-ladder/rung-overflow-natives/probes/compare-normalised.txt`). *Still open, by reading.* Ten natives of the same four files still leave the width without a catchable `IntegerOverflow`: `Int$Pow` and `Int$Choose` go through `Int.rc` (row 347); `Long$Pow` and `Long$Choose` wrap silently; `NN32$Lcm` wraps silently; `NN32$Choose` and `NN32$Pow` go through `NN32.rc`, uncatchable; `UnsignedLong$Lcm`, `$Choose` and `$Pow` wrap silently. `REPORT.md` section 3 lists them. |

